.\" No version in the title line: see the note in irontile.1.
.TH IRONTILE-NOTIFY 1 "" "irontile" "irontile"
.SH NAME
irontile\-notify \- notifications for irontile, and the panel they collect in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B irontile\-notify
.br
.B irontile\-notify
.RB [ \-\-toggle | \-\-open | \-\-close ]
.br
.B irontile\-notify \-\-dump
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-scale
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B irontile\-notify
answers
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
on the session bus, which is how every program on the desktop asks for a word
to appear on screen. What arrives is shown as a card at the corner of the
display and kept in a panel afterwards.
.PP
Started with the session and left running. Only one program at a time may be
the notification daemon: a second one finds the name taken and says so rather
than showing half of everything.
.PP
Popups sit on the overlay layer, above even a fullscreen window, because a
notification nobody can see is a notification that did not happen. They stack
downwards and go on their own after a few seconds \(em except a critical one,
which stays until it is dismissed, since that is the whole of what critical
means.
.PP
The panel is a side panel holding everything that has arrived, with the
session's buttons along the bottom: lock, sleep, hibernate, restart, power off.
Its icons come from the icon theme as SVGs rather than from a font, so a
machine without some particular font still gets pictures \(em and a theme
missing a name still leaves the word underneath saying what the button does.
.PP
Clicking a notification dismisses it. Escape closes the panel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show the panel if it is hidden, hide it if it is shown, and exit. A key press
arrives at the compositor rather than at this program, so a binding runs this
and this asks the running daemon over the bus.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Show the panel.
.TP
.B \-\-close
Hide it.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump " PATH"
Render the popups and the panel to a PNG and exit, without a compositor and
without anything having sent a notification. The only way to work on how these
look without waiting for something to happen.
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
Display scale to render for
.BR \-\-dump .
Default 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-icon\-theme " NAME"
The icon theme to draw from. Default: Adwaita.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start it with the session, and bind the panel to a key:
.PP
.EX
[startup]
exec = [
  "irontile\-notify",
]

[binds]
"Super+n" = "spawn irontile\-notify \-\-toggle"
.EE
.SH BUS
.TP
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
The standard interface, at
.IR /org/freedesktop/Notifications .
Capabilities reported are
.BR actions ,
.BR body ,
.B icon\-static
and
.BR persistence .
.TP
.B org.irontile.Notify1
The panel's own switch, at
.IR /org/irontile/Notify :
.BR Toggle ,
.BR Open ,
.B Close
and
.BR Quiet (b).
Not part of anybody's specification; it exists because a key binding has to
reach a running daemon somehow.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR irontile (1),
.BR irontile\-bar (1),
.BR irontilectl (1)
